      "username": "Rabk",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabk/{size}/1978_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-06-08T20:40:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So a friend has copies of the original 4 promos (YL/HotH/RCWraith/Redeemer) that he doesn't want. They are, of course, the only ones I don't yet have, so I'm going to trade for them out of my overflowing boardgame library. The problem is that I have absolutely no idea what price I shold give him when he starts picking things out. There's a handful of eBay and BGG listings, but a number of them are incomplete/have a bunch of extra stuff/not sold/etc., and I just can't get an idea of whether they're actually worth $5 or $500. He's not attached and isn't interested in putting them on eBay himself (he had no idea they were anything special and initially offerred them to me for far too little), but I want to give him fair value for a relatively rare commodity.&nbsp;</p><p><span>Can anyone offer some help or advice? USD preferred, but I\"m happy to convert from your local currency if needed.</span></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:47:37.378Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
